From: drcano <156254264+drcano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:47:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(disputes): add verify_agent_purchase tool

Given a dispute or capture ID, rebuilds an AI-agent purchase from
PayPal's own records (dispute -> capture -> order -> vault payment
token) and returns the verifier's verdict.

The tool stays thin: the verifier is injected through
context.agentPurchaseVerifier and receives a read-only get() over the
toolkit's authenticated HTTP layer (relative paths only; errors are
returned, not thrown, so the verifier can fail closed). The intended
verifier is verifyCase from @readback/verify@^0.1.0, which is not yet
published; tests use a stub that walks the same chain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
